        "original_id": "bee4ce9b-30b0-509a-b167-b853c65ba6d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. P. Doherty, Debbie Harry, Cyndi Lauper\n- Works: \"Maybe for Sure\", \"Necessary Evil\", \"Def, Dumb & Blonde\"\n- Events: True Colors tour, Necessary Evil tour\n- Topics: Debbie Harry biography\n\nFacts:\n- Deborah Ann Harry, born Angela Tremble on July 1, 1945, is an American singer-songwriter and actress best known as the lead singer of Blondie.\n- Debbie Harry released \"Maybe for Sure\" in 1989 as a single from her third solo album, \"Def, Dumb & Blonde\".\n- In June 2007, J. P. Doherty toured with Debbie Harry on Cyndi Lauper's True Colors tour.\n- In November and December 2007, J. P. Doherty toured with Debbie Harry on the Necessary Evil tour in support of Harry's 2007 release \"Necessary Evil\".",
